/**
@mainpage PebbleOS API Reference

Doxygen-generated reference for the PebbleOS firmware sources.

The public interfaces under @c include are grouped in
<a href="topics.html">Topics</a>, following the include layout:

- @ref kernel — @c pbl/kernel
- @ref mcu — @c pbl/mcu
- @ref soc — @c pbl/soc
- @ref drivers — @c pbl/drivers
- @ref services — @c pbl/services
- @ref subsys — @c pbl/bluetooth, @c pbl/crc, @c pbl/cron, @c pbl/logging,
  @c pbl/shell, @c pbl/task_wdt
- @ref lib — @c pbl/util, @c pbl/btutil
- @ref pebbleos — @c pebbleos

Other indexes:

- <a href="annotated.html">Data Structures</a> — all structs and unions
- <a href="files.html">Files</a> — browse by source tree layout
- <a href="globals_func.html">Functions</a> — flat function index

Source tree overview:

- @c fw/applib — application framework and UI (the app-facing API)
- @c fw/services — system services (bluetooth, filesystem, timers, ...)
- @c fw/kernel — task management, events, memory
- @c fw/drivers — hardware drivers
- @c include — public headers (@c pbl API surface)
- @c lib — shared libraries (util, btutil, c)
- @c subsys — OS subsystems (logging, ...)

For guides and protocol specifications see the
<a href="https://pebbleos-core.readthedocs.io/">PebbleOS documentation</a>.
*/
